From 2609120432139631ef76407a5bbf0d64c1c28349 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iitimii <timiiowolabi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 03:55:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 27/31] S3.2: three-tier routing + conf escalation easy->mid +
 --ttft-opener

Load the easy tier synchronously (front -> easy -> mid, freed in reverse),
always with a checkpoint sequence. Route easy questions to the easy tier
when the bundle has one, hard ones to mid; the front stays the router.

Confidence escalation from an append-only easy tier is checkpoint-provisional:
save a checkpoint, arm the conf monitor (the !append_only restriction is now
lifted only when the caller holds a checkpoint), and on a trigger restore the
state and re-ingest the committed prefix canonically before handing the draft
to mid via the existing carry-draft path.

--ttft-opener streams a front opening segment before the routing decision on
the first turn; the answering tier carries it as a draft. It defaults on only
for a 3-tier registry, so 2-model bundles keep their exact prior behavior.
--codraft-tiers picks the codraft author pair, --temp-easy/--top-p-easy the
easy tier's sampling.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5
